{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>In His image.</b> That it is the image of Elohim. And do not wonder that the creation of the angels was not specified, for Moses our master did not write here about angels, nor about Gehenna, nor about the Account of the Chariot, but only things that we see in the world, as I explained above. Another interpretation: <b>in His image</b> — in His own image, such that He did not need others to lend Him any image." "<b>In the image of Elohim.</b> In the likeness of angels, for the form of angels and of man is the same; and so you shall explain with regard to ״והייתם כאלהים״ (and you shall be like Elohim). And a proof for this: in Bereshit Rabbah they count occurrences of the divine name from בראשית until ולאדם אמר — they are counted. And if you should say that ״בצלם אלהים״ and ״והייתם כאלהים״ are included in the sum of the divine name occurrences, then for you from בראשית until ולאדם אמר there are seventy-three occurrences; rather, certainly they are the language of angels, and therefore the Targum did not render them as in other places. Another interpretation: <b>in the image</b> — a judge and ruler created him. Another interpretation: סרסהו Elohim created him in the image — even though the rest of the creatures were created by the word, man was created in the image, as Rashi explained, in order to give him importance." "<b>Male and female He created them.</b> As the verse explained: ״ויקח אחת מצלעותיו״ (and He took one of his ribs)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The phrase סרסהו is obscure; rendered hyper-literally as left untranslated. It likely relates to a midrashic reading of the verse's unusual forms, possibly connected to the word סריס (eunuch) or a rearrangement of letters, but the text is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:20:03.912223317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}